window.BODY_I18N["report-2026-11-21-09-snowfall-review-criteria"]=Object.assign({},window.BODY_I18N["report-2026-11-21-09-snowfall-review-criteria"]||{},{"en": "# Life in the Jungle | Divided views on the film \"폭설\": ask what its perspective promises, not how hard its twists hit\n\n**Published: November 21, 2026 | Event/data basis: November 20 film commentary; reported release on November 18 | Checked: November 21, 00:45 KST**\n**By: 데일리샷 매크로 리서치**\n\n![3D conceptual illustration. Not a photograph of an actual event or person.](images/nov21-09-3d.jpg)\n\n*3D conceptual illustration, not a photograph of an actual event or person. See the article for figures, conditions and sources.*\n\n## We do not claim to have watched the film\n\nThe movie segment of Maebul Show released on the 20th revealed different evaluation criteria for the new film \"폭설.\" This article examines criticism by reviewing the broadcast's complete automatic transcript and cross-checking publicly available dialogue from the distributor's trailer. It is not this publication's review of the feature film after watching it. Because the automatic transcript contains errors in personal and proper names, statements have not been quoted verbatim or detailed sentences definitively assigned to individual panelists.[1][2]\n\nThe trailer briefly presents a person arriving at a quiet location, a locked door, suspicion and confrontation. It is not a source containing every piece of information or every relationship in the film. The trailer alone cannot justify judging the ending or writing as though scenes mentioned in the broadcast were watched firsthand.[2]\n\n## Fair clues and concentrated tension\n\nOne strand of criticism in the broadcast concerns whether viewers can fairly connect the clues in retrospect. Another asks whether overlapping devices, shifting perspectives and tension between two characters disrupt concentration. These are not discussions that can all end with the same rating of \"not entertaining.\" They differ in what they regard as the film's promise.[1]\n\nWhat follows is this publication's interpretation of that difference. Viewers who approach a mystery as a puzzle may prioritize the placement of information and consistency of the solution. Those who see it as anxiety and a struggle for power between characters may care more about whom they follow and what they are kept from knowing. The same delay in information can look unfair to the former and create tension for the latter. Without watching the feature, however, we cannot decide which approach this film actually executes better.\n\n## The number of twists is not a scorecard\n\nMany twists are evidence neither of quality nor of failure. More specific questions are whether they change how earlier scenes are seen, connect with characters' choices, and remain consistent with information given to the audience. Turning the broadcast debate into those questions helps viewers prepare their own response rather than simply adopting one side.\n\nPanelists' attendance forecasts must also be distinguished from results. Box-office predictions offered in the broadcast are opinions about the future, not final admissions or confirmed performance. This article does not give unverified cumulative admissions, a break-even point, or screening and streaming availability.\n\n## Two lines to write after watching\n\nReaders who have watched the film can first note what they felt it promised. They can then choose one scene in which that promise seemed fulfilled or broken. This helps separate being surprised by a twist from judging it persuasive.\n\nThe value of criticism is not confined to assigning stars on an audience's behalf. When different reviews reveal what they are looking at, disagreements in taste become a more explainable conversation. This broadcast is a starting point for reading those differences, not a substitute for a conclusion about a film one has not yet watched.\n\n## Sources\n[1] Podbbang Maebul Show, [1120-2,3] Cinema Hell, 2026-11-20. Meaning of the complete automatic transcript reviewed; not all original audio listened to. Relevant episode information and audio source checked through the program API. https://app-api6.podbbang.com/channels/16898/episodes?offset=0&limit=5&sort=desc\n[2] SHOWBOX, main trailer for \"폭설.\" Public dialogue transcript checked; not the feature film. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UFMBTPqJ5Hk\n"});
